---
// A quotation from an official document, word for word. Props only, and used by
// the results page alone: it carries program data, so the questionnaire must
// never reach it, directly or through another component (INV-01).
//
// No maximum height, no ellipsis, no line clamp: a shortened quote is an altered
// quote, and the quote is the evidence the product rests on (INV-06). The serif
// and the vertical rule come from the blockquote rule of styles.css, where the
// family is a provenance marker rather than a decoration (C2).
//
// The quotation stays in the language of its document at every interface
// language, and no translation is put in its place: a translated quotation is
// no longer the text the CI checks word for word, so the evidence would be gone
// (INV-06, DP-18, C4). The language attribute is what keeps it intelligible to
// an English reader's screen reader — read with English rules, French is not
// merely imperfect but unusable (WCAG 3.1.2).
import { CORPUS_LANG } from "../lib/ui.js";

const { text } = Astro.props;
---

<blockquote lang={CORPUS_LANG}>« {text} »</blockquote>
